  [C4 — THE RENAMING GROUP.  The layer's labels are the two
   actor names and the two proposal values; every vertex name
   is BUILT from them by d42b3's own `vname` recursion, so a
   label map determines a map on vertices, on triples, on
   events and on histories.  The group is the four label maps
   (actor swap) x (value flip); each one is CHECKED here to be
   a weight-preserving bijection of the family that commutes
   with the record functor and preserves mu_Zhat.  SCOPE: this
   is the RENAMING group.  A hypothetical automorphism of the
   weighted layer not of label-map form is out of scope and is
   named as a residue, not assumed away.]
  [PASS] F0(i) THE RENAMING GROUP IS COMPUTED, NOT ASSUMED: the four label maps act on the whole family as WEIGHT-PRESERVING bijections (every history's renamed menu equals the menu of its renamed history, weight by weight), they carry record classes to record classes bijectively at every depth, and they preserve mu_Zhat.  The group is NOT trivial and it is NOT free: the fixed-point census is printed  (violations = 0; record-class permutation failures = 0; histories MOVED per generator = [('id', 0), ('value-flip', 34248), ('actor-swap', 34374), ('both', 34374)] (of 34375))
