[F1 — THE CONSTRAINT SYSTEM.  Every convention printed; both
 C1 readings carried; C3 operationalised and gated.]
  VARIABLES.  D is a form on the depth-D history layer.  The
  headline space is REAL SYMMETRIC over Q: one variable per
  UNORDERED pair {h, h'} (diagonal included), so D(h,h') =
  D(h',h) holds by construction.  The HERMITIAN extension is
  carried as a SEPARATE COLUMN: D = S + iA with S symmetric
  and A antisymmetric over Q, one variable per unordered pair
  h != h', reported as `asym` throughout.
  C1 — THREE READINGS, ALL CARRIED; THE MIDDLE ONE IS THE
  HEADLINE (round-1 BLOCKER 1).
    (medium, FAITHFUL — paper 29 §4.3 hypothesis 2 + §3.1's
     pushforward, and the ONLY one of the three that is a
     stated condition of the parent paper)
              Dbar(r,r') = sum_{h in r, h' in r'} D(h,h')
                         = delta_{rr'} . mu_Zhat(r)
            — the coarse-grained functional on the record
            algebra is DIAGONAL and its diagonal is the record
            measure: medium decoherence, the condition that
            licenses a scalar probability for a record class.
    (sum, WEAKER BOUND)   for every record class r at depth D:
              sum_{h,h' in r} D(h,h')  =  mu_Zhat(r)
            — the r = r' half of the faithful condition and
            NOTHING ELSE.  It DROPS DECOHERENCE ENTIRELY: the
            queried algebra is never asked to decohere, so no
            scalar record probability is licensed for the
            object it constrains.  Carried as a lower bound.
    (block, STRICTER BOUND) D(h,h') = 0 whenever record(h) !=
            record(h'), and sum_{h in r} D(h,h) = mu_Zhat(r)
            — vanishing ENTRY BY ENTRY at the FINE level.  It
            implies the faithful condition and is strictly
            stronger: it FORBIDS BY HAND, one level down and
            before any row is written, the cancellations that
            coarse decoherence explicitly permits.  Carried as
            an upper bound.
  C3 — CYLINDER CONSISTENCY, operationalised.  A depth-d
  history g denotes the cylinder of its depth-D extensions, so
  the restricted form is
      R^(d)(g,g') = sum over depth-D a extending g,
                         depth-D b extending g'   of  D(a,b)
  (paper 29 §4.2's additive restriction, and §3's `a depth-d
  cylinder is the union of its extensions').  C3 demands that
  R^(D-1) satisfy THE SAME convention's C1 at depth D-1 —
  that is the pin's ONE DEPTH STEP.  The FULL-CHAIN variant,
  demanding it at every d = D-1 ... 0, is carried alongside.
  C4 — equivariance is imposed BY CONSTRUCTION: with C4 on,
  the variables are the RENAMING-GROUP ORBITS of pairs, which
  is exactly the invariant subspace.  C4 off is carried too.
  NOTE, and it is the reason C3 has content: the record
  functor does NOT commute with taking prefixes.  Two
  serialisations of one labelled DAG have DIFFERENT prefix
  records, so the depth-D record partition is not a refinement
  of the depth-(D-1) one and C1 at depth D does not imply C1
  at depth D-1.  This is gated below.
  [PASS] F1(a) THE C3 OPERATIONALISATION REDUCES TO THE CLASSICAL MARGINAL ON DIAGONAL MEMBERS [the pin's own gate on the definition]: for a DIAGONAL form with weights w, the restricted form R^(d) is again diagonal and its entries are exactly the cylinder marginals sum_{a extends g} w(a) — checked at every depth step of every truncation, for mu_Zhat AND for a deliberately non-classical index-weighted diagonal (so the check cannot pass on mu's own symmetry)  (40 (truncation, weighting, step) combinations, marginal mismatches = 0)
  [PASS] F1(b) THE RECORD FUNCTOR DOES NOT COMMUTE WITH PREFIXES, AND IT DOES NOT SPLIT EVERYTHING EITHER — the two-sided fact that gives C3 its content and then leaves something over [SUBSTANTIVE]: some record classes' members carry DIFFERENT parent records (two serialisations of one labelled DAG that the previous cut could already tell apart) and some do not.  Because the first set is non-empty, the depth-D record partition is NOT the pullback of the depth-(D-1) one and C1 at depth D carries no C1 at depth D-1: C3 is an independent demand, not bookkeeping.  Because the second set is non-empty, C3 cannot kill every coherence — which is exactly the shape of the F4 answer  (multi-member record classes across the truncations = 4735, of which prefix-record-SPLITTING = 2839; within-class unordered pairs with DIFFERENT parent records = 73674, with the SAME parent record = 88036)
  [PASS] F1(c) NO TWO SIBLINGS SHARE A RECORD [SUBSTANTIVE, and it is what makes the block convention's C3 rows readable]: within a record class no two distinct members have the SAME depth-(D-1) prefix, so every within-class off-diagonal entry is an entry between two histories with DISTINCT parents  (same-parent within-class ordered pairs = 0)
