  [THE FORCING MECHANISM under the BLOCK reading, one-step C3.
   A within-class entry D(h,h') survives into the depth-(D-1)
   restriction as a term of R^(D-1)(g,g'), g and g' the two
   parents.  By F1(c) the parents are distinct; by F1(b) they
   usually carry DIFFERENT records, and then the block reading
   demands R^(D-1)(g,g') = 0.  The question is how many terms
   that row has.]
