  [THE WITNESSES.  For every configuration with a non-zero
   coherence dimension, an EXACT member is constructed by
   perturbing the classical member along a kernel direction
   with value 1 at a free within-class coherence coordinate.
   The scale t is DERIVED — t = (smallest diagonal entry) /
   (2 x largest absolute row-sum of the direction) — so the
   perturbed matrix is STRICTLY DIAGONALLY DOMINANT with a
   positive diagonal, hence positive definite by Gershgorin,
   with an exact rational certificate and no eigenvalue.]
  [PASS] F4(d) THE COHERENCE WITNESS EXISTS AND IS EXHIBITED [the pin's sharpest question, answered POSITIVELY]: for every configuration with cohdim > 0 at truncation depth <= 4, an exact member is constructed with a NON-ZERO within-class off-diagonal entry; it satisfies EVERY constraint row exactly (zero residual) and is certified POSITIVE DEFINITE by exact strict diagonal dominance over Q.  Superposition between histories the record cannot distinguish is PERMITTED by these record demands at this scope.  HONESTY, round-1 MINOR 7: this is ONE ALGORITHM RUN AT N CONFIGURATIONS — classical + t x (kernel direction at the first free coherence column in a fixed column order), same derived t — not N independent pieces of evidence  (witnesses built = 28, witnesses failing a row or the positivity certificate = 0)

